#, python-format
msgid ""
"La curva OC de los planes por atributos (y los planes de Dodge-Romig) usa"
" la distribución **binomial** (curva tipo B: el lote sale de un proceso "
"con fracción defectiva `p`), como las tablas de las normas. Para un lote "
"finito aislado (tipo A) lo exacto es la hipergeométrica, que da una "
"probabilidad de aceptación algo menor (`N = 1000`, `n = 132`, `c = 3` y 5"
" % defectuosos: binomial 0,0992 frente a hipergeométrica 0,0838)."
msgstr ""
"The OC curve of the plans by attributes (and the Dodge-Romig plans) uses "
"the **binomial** distribution (type B curve: the lot comes from a process"
" with defective fraction `p`), like the tables of the standards. For an "
"isolated finite lot (type A) the exact one is the hypergeometric, which "
"gives a slightly lower acceptance probability (`N = 1000`, `n = 132`, `c "
"= 3` and 5 % defective: binomial 0.0992 versus hypergeometric 0.0838)."

