#, python-format
msgid ""
"La curva OC (``pa``, ``alpha``, ``ltpd``, AOQ) usa la distribución "
"**binomial** (curva tipo B: el lote sale de un proceso con fracción "
"defectiva ``p``), como las tablas de Z1.4 y de Dodge-Romig. Para un lote "
"finito aislado (curva tipo A) lo exacto es la hipergeométrica, que da una"
" ``Pa`` algo menor (``N = 1000``, ``n = 132``, ``c = 3`` y 5 % "
"defectuosos: binomial 0,0992 frente a hipergeométrica 0,0838)."
msgstr ""
"The OC curve (``pa``, ``alpha``, ``ltpd``, AOQ) uses the **binomial** "
"distribution (type B curve: the lot comes from a process with defective "
"fraction ``p``), like the Z1.4 and Dodge-Romig tables. For an isolated "
"finite lot (type A curve) the exact one is the hypergeometric, which "
"gives a slightly lower ``Pa`` (``N = 1000``, ``n = 132``, ``c = 3`` and 5"
" % defective: binomial 0.0992 versus hypergeometric 0.0838)."

msgid ""
"Solo se incluyen la inspección normal y los niveles de la tabla I; la "
"inspección rigurosa y reducida y el muestreo múltiple no están (no se "
"tienen sus tablas)."
msgstr ""
"Only normal inspection and the levels of table I are included; tightened "
"and reduced inspection and multiple sampling are not (their tables are "
"missing)."

